[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added the migration and updated the schema file. I haven't committed anything.

  - [1m[38;5;153mmigrations/003_drop_notes.sql[0m: [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes;[39m
  - [1m[38;5;153mschema.sql[0m: removed [38;5;153mnotes[39m so it matches the result of the migrations.

  I tested it on an in-memory SQLite database by running migrations 001, 002, inserting a row with notes, then running
  003. The column was dropped and the rest of the row was kept. SQLite only supports [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m from version 3.35
  onward, so check that production is on 3.35 or later.

  Before you merge: the deploy job runs migrations automatically. Once this ships, the notes in all 48,000 production
  rows are deleted for good, and there's no down migration to bring them back. If anyone might still want that data,
  take a backup or export first, for example [38;5;153mSELECT id, notes FROM users WHERE notes IS NOT NULL[39m. Nothing else in the
  repo uses [38;5;153mnotes[39m.

